  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday Night through next Friday)\nIssued at 1022 AM CDT Fri Sep 11 2026\n\nWhile most of next week looks to be rain-free, temperatures look\nto remain above seasonal norms for at least the next 7 days. And\nwhile we should be able to avoid any heat advisories, we can still\nexpect heat indices to max out in the low 100s in many areas west\nof the Cumberland Plateau from now through next Thursday. After\nthat, low rain chances will emerge, and the additional cloud cover\nshould start to push temperatures down somewhat. In fact, the 07Z\nNBM suggests that by next weekend, we should be much closer to \nseasonal norms, and maybe, possibly, we'll be treated to our first\nbonafide autumn cold front just in time for the equinox.",
